# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, R-4, R-5; the lead's fix 2). L §5.14: "The batch's arrivals are supplies. Parts that arrive at
# x in the same batch are supplies of its takes"; "A movement's take never includes its own arrivals"; a relabel "takes
# parts by the leaving rule and returns them labelled by the arrival rule, batches kept". A relabel's arrival is an
# arrival of its batch, so it is a supply of the batch's other outflows at the place.
# The gift g (giver tomek) takes 40.00 of tomek's (its order ranks the giver's parts first); its arrival is ania's, by
# the rule, which reads no take, so it is a supply of s1 at once: s1's 120.00 takes ania's 100.00 and 20.00 of the gift's
# ania 40.00 (ania 20.00, tomek 10.00; scratch/expfix2.py).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind couples: parties
kind savings: place PLN min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w order if w in gifts and k.owner == w.giver then 0 else 1, if k.owner == ania then 0 else 1
kind gifts: transfers
  attr giver: key persons
  attr receiver: key persons
kind tomeks: transfers
place konto: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input a1_day: date
input a1_amt: money PLN
input t1_day: date
input t1_amt: money PLN
input g_day: date
input g_amt: money PLN
input s1_day: date
input s1_amt: money PLN
def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule base = if p == ania then 1 else 0
  rule t beats base = if p == tomek then 1 else 0 when m in tomeks
  rule gift beats base, t = if p == m.receiver then 1 else 0 when m in gifts
move a1: transfers
  on a1_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount a1_amt
move t1: tomeks
  on t1_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount t1_amt
move g: gifts
  on g_day
  attr giver = tomek
  attr receiver = ania
  leg cash from konto to konto amount g_amt
move s1: transfers
  on s1_day
  leg cash from konto to shop amount s1_amt
ask q: bal(konto, 2026-03-01), bal(konto, 2026-03-01) of ania, bal(konto, 2026-03-01) of tomek, g.cash.amount of tomek

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2010-06-01..
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  a1_day = 2026-02-01
  a1_amt = 100.00 PLN
  t1_day = 2026-02-02
  t1_amt = 50.00 PLN
  g_day = 2026-03-01
  g_amt = 40.00 PLN
  s1_day = 2026-03-01
  s1_amt = 120.00 PLN
=== expect
q: (30.00 PLN, 20.00 PLN, 10.00 PLN, 40.00 PLN)
  cut 2026-01-01
